From 730bacb56a333bbfacafd1651f6ce36cedbaec9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:00:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DNN strong branching (sb.*): the branching line from the
 children's DNN bounds

At a branching node of depth sb.depths that kept its DNN state, the children of
the candidate lines (the sb.k rows and columns with the largest marginal scores,
or every free line through depth sb.all; a row's real children only where
symmetry is left) are bounded with sb.iters warm ADMM iterations, and the node
branches on the line whose children's shortfalls give the least sum of
shortfall^P (sb.power by depth: the 8th power at the root, the sum below).
sb.gap = D:G gates it by the relative gap of the node's own DNN bound. Off by
default: without sb.depths the tree is node for node what it was (nug20, nug22
with the nug30 recipe; bench check, resume, parallel, coordinator, node-trace and
ship tests pass).

Its cost is the run's own: the RESULTS head gets "strong branch: N nodes, S child
solves, I iterations, T s" and a table by level, kept in state files (QAP-STATE
10: sb_n_level, sb_s_level, sb_i_level, sb_t_level; versions 1-9 still read) and
summed by bench/parallel.py and the coordinator.

QAP_SB_TRACE: a line per strong-branching node. QAP_SB_PROGRESS: child solves
appended to a file and reused after a restart. tests/sb_test.py (make sb):
statistics against the trace, the progress file, parallel totals, the gate,
refused settings. RUNNING.md: "DNN strong branching (sb.*)".

Measurements: experiments/branching_lab/root and experiments/branching_lab/port
(branch claude/cool-babbage-ilnogj).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014vvMYV3r6FDoHTc2G3VVqC
